    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1206">

                <pb facs="0852" n="736" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg736"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/223.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Hostetter to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 637.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate.</hi>
                            <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Hermosillo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-03-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 17, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of the Department’s telegram March 16, regarding the collection of
                    mining taxes by the Constitutionalists after having once been paid to the
                    Federals. I had same complaint upon the return of General Carranza from Sinaloa
                    and he, at the time, promised to look into the matter, although he held he had a
                    right to demand the payment of the same. I told him according and agreeable to
                    international law, it was not right to demand this payment, as a government in
                    power had a right to collect these same taxes. It is possible, that on account
                    of his constant moving, he forgot to look into the matter. I have wired to
                    Juarez in regard to the matter.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Louis Hostetter</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
